croenvironment during ICI therapy remains unaddressed in the literature. The available evidence relies on fecal measurements, occasional serum data, and preclinical models rather than intratumoral sampling.\n\nI should note that none of these sources report absolute concentration values with specific units, so I cannot extract quantitative comparisons. The usable content should emphasize this methodological gap while documenting what measurement approaches have been attempted (fecal sampling, serum analysis, mouse models) and where the limitations lie.",
